 so looks a  little thicker and I wanted that because  the leather is used on the shoe  represents more of like a boot leather  there are four laces that come with the  shoe the first one is the beige in  burgundy that comes tied in and then the  other three options are burgundy olive  olive off-white and then an all-white  place I don't believe that people know  what goes behind making specific product  you know we just see the end result or  the consumer sees the end result but  they're not they're at the factory  seeing how things are made and on this  asymmetrical piece there's this faux  stitch that kind of finishes the mock  that goes all the way around having to  stitch it over the shoe and then stitch  around the mock to really finish it off  it was a little bit of an issue in the  beginning and it was a big design  element that I wanted to implement so we  went back and forth until they got it  right I'm seeing a lot of companies  suffer in terms of quality control the  investment that Diadora has made into  factories in Italy is is unprecedented  they wouldn't be possible if it wasn't  handmade in Italy you know they're  perfect
 

